From: fedoraforsnapdragon <52586739+Dudiebug@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus13-spi-touch: power the touchscreen at probe

The 15-inch GPIO power description (patches/0005) links the GTCH
touchscreen to the eDP panel, and spi-hid (patches/0004) then powers it
only when the display driver enables that panel. At the 13.8-inch unit's
first boot the display stayed on the UEFI framebuffer (msm never took
over), so the touchscreen was never powered and stayed silent.

Drop the panel link on the 13.8-inch SPI-touchscreen tree: spi-hid then
powers and resets the GTCH at probe and handles system sleep itself, as
it does for the touchpad. The 15-inch tree keeps the link. Restore it
here once msm drives this panel and the touchscreen answers.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13-spi-touch.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13-spi-touch.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13-spi-touch.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13-spi-touch.dts
@@ -33,3 +33,12 @@ &iris {

 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * Power the touchscreen at probe instead of following the eDP panel: on this
+ * unit the display driver has not taken over yet, and a follower is then never
+ * powered. The 15-inch tree keeps the panel link.
+ */
+&gtch {
+	/delete-property/ panel;
+};
